## Re-filing

A borrower or confirmed successor whose further extension request on a Cedarline Summit loan's Maturity and Due-and-Payable Cases case rests on supporting evidence that is no longer current re-files it in person with current evidence.

- The re-filed request is recorded as received on the day it is filed.
- It states the number of further extension days it asks for.
- The earlier request stays on file, while any grant rests on the most recently received request awaiting a decision.

Among extension requests received on the same day, the more recently received is the one recorded later by its recorded date and time. A request re-filed on the day of the request it replaces is therefore the one a grant rests on.

| After re-filing | Status on the case |
|---|---|
| the earlier request | stays on file |
| the re-filed request | received on the filing day, awaiting a decision, carrying its supporting document and that document's date |
| the request a grant rests on | the most recently received one awaiting a decision, which is the re-filed request |

## Filing the request: `supplement_extension_request_11bdc0c2`

**Capability.** One call files a new extension request from the caller for the same case, in place of the pending request named. The new request:

- is dated today, with status received;
- carries the supporting document supplied and the number of extension days asked for.

The earlier request is left on file unchanged. The requested extension days form part of the new request's reference number. They are printed on the receipt together with the deadline they would reach. The request lookup then shows the new request next to the earlier one.

**Invocation.** This is the customer's own tool. The agent unlocks `supplement_extension_request_11bdc0c2` and hands it over, and the customer themselves runs it in person.

**Parameters.**

| Parameter | Meaning | Format |
|---|---|---|
| `maturity_case_id` | reference number of the maturity case, read by the agent from the maturity case lookup and given to the caller | identifier |
| `maturity_request_id` | reference number of the caller's pending extension request this filing takes the place of, read from the maturity request lookup | identifier |
| `customer_id` | the caller's own customer reference number, read from the customer lookup | identifier |
| `evidence_type` | kind of supporting document | exactly one of the values listed below |
| `evidence_reference` | the reference printed on the supporting document (commitment letter number or listing agreement number) | verbatim, character for character |
| `evidence_date` | the date printed on the supporting document | YYYY-MM-DD, no time or time zone |
| `requested_extension_days` | whole number of calendar days the request asks to add to the case's current resolution deadline | integer of 0 or more, no unit text, no decimals |

The `evidence_type` values are:

- `listing_agreement`: a signed listing agreement with a real estate broker;
- `financing_commitment`: a lender's written financing commitment for the purchase or refinance;
- `reoccupancy_certification`: not evidence for an extension;
- `repayment_receipt`: not evidence for an extension;
- `repair_inspection`: not evidence for an extension;
- `recorded_deed`: not evidence for an extension;
- `failed_condition_inspection`: not evidence for an extension;
- `not_applicable`: no supporting document at all.

**Return.** A text rendering of a record with these fields:

- `maturity_request_id`, the new request's reference;
- `replaced_request_id`;
- `maturity_case_id`;
- `request_date`, today;
- `evidence_type`;
- `evidence_reference`;
- `evidence_date`;
- `requested_extension_days`;
- `requested_through_date`, the current resolution deadline moved later by the requested days.

A receipt with a new request reference number means the request is filed and awaiting a decision. An unknown case reference returns an error naming it.
